1... Ra8 2. a4 { White's best move was } (2. b3 Nxd2 3. Qxd2 Ra3 { and Black would ultimately win the a-pawn, always keeping a slight advantage in position. }) 2... Nxd2 3. Qxd2 Qc4 4. Rfd1 Reb8 { Black could have regained the Pawn by playing 4...Bxc3, but he sees that there is more to be had, and therefore increases the pressure against White's Queen side. He now threatens, among other things, ...Rxb2. } 5. Qe3 Rb4 { Threatening to win the exchange by ...Bd4 } 6. Qg5 Bd4+ 7. Kh1 Rab8 { This threatens to win the Knight, and thus forces White to give up the exchange. } 8. Rxd4 Qxd4 9. Rd1 Qc5 { Now Black will recover his Pawn. } *


