{ The climax of the combination started with }
1. Bh4 Qd7 { White is still threatening mate, and the best way to avoid it is for Black to give back all the material he has gained and to remain three Pawns behind. } 2. Nxc8 Qxc6 3. Qd8+ Qe8 { If: } (3... Kf7 4. Nd6+ { King moves, and White mates. }) 4. Be7+ Kf7 5. Nd6+ Kg6 6. Nh4+ Kh5 { If: } (6... Kh6 7. Ndf5+ Kh5 8. Nxg7+ Kh6 9. Nhf5+ Kg6 10. Qd6+ { and mate next move. }) 7. Nxe8 Rxd8 8. Nxg7+ Kh6 9. Ngf5+ Kh5 10. h3! *


